It builds on:

TensorFold
  https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold
  Copyright 2026 TensorFold contributors. Apache License 2.0. engine/engine.sh clones it (main 9ccf4727) and merges
  pull request #727's head (6e95bc6d), jayleaton's DeepSeek-V4.1 series, which keeps its authors' notices.

deepseek-v41-tensorfold-spark
  https://github.com/jayleaton/deepseek-v41-tensorfold-spark
  Copyright 2026 Jay Leaton (https://x.com/jayleaton). Apache License 2.0.
  Included unmodified as the git submodule vendor/deepseek-v41-tensorfold-spark; its NOTICE applies to it.
  - engine/engine.sh copies the files engine/kit-overlay.txt lists from its engine/zig snapshot.
  - engine/patches/ modify those files and TensorFold's: the kit engine on TensorFold main's APIs, native images on
    main's server, the 1017 pack's fp16 tensors, and video input (Apache-2.0, section 4).
  - docker/Dockerfile is its docker/zig/Dockerfile with this engine's binaries and libtfvideo added.
  - config/native.env.example is its config/prod-zig.env.example with this recipe's values.

xgrammar (vendored in engine/patches by the kit engine's in-process structured output)
  https://github.com/mlc-ai/xgrammar, Apache License 2.0; its license and notice travel with it.

FFmpeg (built into libtfvideo by docker/Dockerfile through TensorFold's tools/zig/build_ffmpeg.sh)
  https://ffmpeg.org, LGPL-2.1-or-later as TensorFold configures it.

Model weights are not included; scripts/stage.sh downloads them from Hugging Face:
  deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 (MIT, DeepSeek): the Engram tables and the image routing bias;
  LibertAIDAI/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.9bpw (MIT): the EXL3 pack;
  Mia-AiLab/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-EXL3-2.9bpw (MIT): its chat_template.jinja.
